Z||000000||jazer||10-16-2000||07:04 PM||||I've got a guy who'll put a 4.3l in my 87 4cyl Fiero.  I'm going to put a 5-speed Getrag in.  Would it be worth doing? Will the motor bolt up?  Comments would be greatly apreciated. Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||10-16-2000||07:07 PM||||it's just as easy to put in a SBC 350.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-16-2000||07:16 PM||||Enjoy the rewiring!  84 is 4cylinder wiring, so lots of fun with the wires in front of the engine.  I hope your "guy" knows what he's doing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||10-16-2000||08:49 PM||||Go for it. You'll be among the first. Then tell the rest of us what you had to do.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>It's gotta be a pain. You'll need most of a V-8 Archie kit, and will have to do some fabricating. (I don't know what all...) No Fiero trans will bolt up without an adapter. A lot of us have discussed this (try running a search on 4.3) and I think someone is in the middle of the swap, but most folks are just not willing to expend the time and funds. There are a number of swaps that will provide more "bang for the buck."<BR>And that doesn't even touch on the ECM/EFI stuff. <BR>Good luck with your project. And welcome to the Forum.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-16-2000||11:59 PM||||I've got a 4.3L sitting in my carport right now....  I'm just trying to get the NERVE to try the swap!!  I want to try the 4.3L along with a turbo setup like the GMC Syclone/typhone was...   Welcome to the forum...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  This is the best place on the net fer' Fiero information, thank's to Mr. Cliff.   :;            Steve<BR>                         1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||msweldon||10-17-2000||09:16 AM||||I'm no engine swap guru, but I did look into this somewhat seriously about a year and a half ago.  I too wanted that Cyclone setup in my fiero.  280hp 300ft/lbs oooooooooohhh!!! <BR>However, I chose not to because of the following.<BR>1. The 4.3 is a longitude mount engine(an SBC with two cylinders loped off)<BR>2. I wanted to keep from chopping my frame and fabricating parts.<BR>3. I wanted to keep as much of the same fiero running gear as possible.<BR> <BR>(After becoming a member here I learned that)<BR>Ed Parks can install a 3.6L(overbored 3.4) w/ mods right into the fiero with little effort. ~$3300 entire swap.  And with a properly built turbo system (see 1FST2M6) you could easily net the same numbers as the 4.3 Turbo cyclone with the added benefit of very little modifications, same engine weight, and a stock look.  <P>Also, if I can recall correctly, not all 4.3's were the same.  The turbo Vortec V6 on the Cyclones/Typhoons had "many" hi-po components to take the added stress of forced induction.<P>But hey...if you have loads of money to burn and/or a "crack" mechanic at hand, have a ball and let me know how that 300hp V6 feels.<P>hope this helps,<BR>marc||||reg||1
